      "hints": [
        "Integrate $8(2x-3)^{1/3}$ to get $3(2x-3)^{4/3}$ and $-10x^{2/3}$ to get $-6x^{5/3}$.",
        "Add a constant of integration $+ C$.",
        "Substitute $(1, 0)$ into $f(x)$ to solve for $C$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate $f'(x) = 8(2x-3)^{1/3} - 10x^{2/3}$ with respect to $x$:\n$$f(x) = \\int \\left( 8(2x - 3)^{1/3} - 10x^{2/3} \\right) dx = \\frac{8(2x - 3)^{4/3}}{\\frac{4}{3} \\times 2} - \\frac{10x^{5/3}}{\\frac{5}{3}} + C = 3(2x - 3)^{4/3} - 6x^{5/3} + C$$",
        "Use the boundary condition $f(1) = 0$ to solve for $C$:\n$$0 = 3(2(1) - 3)^{4/3} - 6(1)^{5/3} + C = 3(-1)^{4/3} - 6(1) + C$$\n$$\\text{Since } (-1)^{4/3} = ((-1)^4)^{1/3} = 1: \\quad 0 = 3(1) - 6 + C = -3 + C \\implies C = 3$$",
        "State the full function $f(x)$:\n$$f(x) = 3(2x - 3)^{4/3} - 6x^{5/3} + 3$$"
      ],
